# A reference formal `@: Model v` rebound to an Other of another shape (two ints, no size_t `value` in its place): the
# admission of o to Model refuses it -- the method's implicit throw `implements`, uncaught, stops R0
# (OPUS-CALLABLE-STRUCT-BINDING-20260929-16).  It was a plain store, and the path through v read the Other's cell.
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

Other:
    int: p 1
    int: q 2
end: Other

fn: m (@: Model v) int
    o: merge Other
    size_t: got 0U
    int: out 0
    o\p: 41
    v: o
    got: v\value
    if: got = 41U
        out: 7
    return: out
end: m

fn: check () int
    mo: merge Model
return: m(mo)

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
